13:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"cpu_count"}]," is what the shipped README passes. The scheduler declares it as a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"minimum"}]," platform property and the worker advertises it from ",["$","code",null,{"children":"nproc"}],", so an\naction is only matched to a worker with at least that many cores; ask for more\nthan the worker has and the action queues silently forever. Omitting the\nproperty is fine: an action with no platform properties matches any worker. See\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"platform properties"}],"."]}]
