23:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"worker.json5"}]," sets ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_namespaces: true"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_mount_namespace: true"}],",\nwhich need ",["$","code",null,{"children":"CLONE_NEWUSER"}],"/",["$","code",null,{"children":"CLONE_NEWNS"}],", hence the flag. Note what this buys\nand what it does not: namespaces here are a hermeticity and process-reaping\nmechanism, not a security boundary. Actions still run as the worker's own uid\nthrough an identity uid map, still see the host filesystem apart from a\nprivate ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}],", and still have network access to every Forge port. A\nprivileged container running\narbitrary build actions is a lateral-movement primitive.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/security-hardening#the-sandbox-is-not-a-security-boundary","children":"Security hardening"}],"\ncovers what the sandbox actually does."]}]
